
# Implementation Plan - Curriculum Metrics Glue Job

This plan outlines the creation of a strictly optimized AWS Glue job to calculate text metrics for curriculum learning on ~1TB of data.

## Goal Description
Create a standalone Glue script that processes ~1TB of raw JSON.gz data to produce two distinct outputs:
1.  **Team 1 Output**: Converted Parquet files retaining the original input folder structure (1-to-1 mapping of dataset folders).
2.  **Team 2 Output**: A separate metrics-only Parquet dataset, partitioned by `domain` and `external_source`.

The script must prioritize efficiency, avoiding Python UDFs where possible, using short-circuit logic for rejections, and managing memory carefully to avoid OOM.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Output Structure**:
> - Team 1: `s3://.../team1_output/<dataset_name>/` (Parquet, ~128MB partitions)
> - Team 2: `s3://.../team2_output/domain=<domain>/external_source=<source>/`
>
> **Dependencies**: The script requires `tiktoken` for token counting. This must be passed via `--additional-python-modules`. A `README.md` will be provided with instructions.

